Separate backend catalog/selection/todo facts from local selector controls. Cover command/file catalogs and generations, model/provider/variant/execution-reasoning choices, agent selection where applicable, session/user-turn pickers, todos and workspace metadata. Publish backend-affecting facts that are or may become visible through focused UnlockedData/projections where bounded existing domains permit. Discovery, source authority and validated backend selection mutations remain backend-owned. Establish actual active-agent authority and selection writers with /03; a picker highlight is not the agent receiving next Enter.

Formatting, filtering, search text, highlight, scroll, open/close state, previews and UI-only theme/settings choices live in tui-specific files on the tui-thread without locks/UnlockedData. Draft text remains exclusively frontend-owned until submitted as a string. Selector actions use validated identifiers and publish resulting backend facts rather than returning replacement SelectListView bundles. Preserve unknown/loading/error/empty semantics, generations, no-op work avoidance and valid selection on refresh; invalidate stale entries safely. Execution reasoning/model variants are backend facts, display-only reasoning controls are local.

Do not solve large backend list/vector access in this iteration or copy large lists every render. Preserve existing history-backed user-turn/session-content and applicable inspector/streaming paths as an explicitly inventoried deferred exception; future collection access needs separate design, not a journal or history migration here. Distinguish retained content from ordinary backend metadata/selected values, which must migrate. Remove superseded ordinary views/options and verify generations, errors, stale selections, model bulk actions, session navigation, todos and fork/copy authorization with selector/completion/render tests and real terminal selector scenarios. Preserve functionality and path/permission authority throughout.

